[anicel 0005] windows: make the EGL display anew when its context is lost

Board a-real-gpu-reset-went-unheard-on-the-main-pc, step two.

A loss is told once (0002 posts it to the process's windows), and the
engine then restores on the platform thread, in this order: the raster
thread is asked whether it answers at all (2 s; one stuck in the driver
is left as it is), the compositor hears, the engine lets go (0004), what
the views and textures hold of the lost display is forgotten without a
call to EGL, the display and its contexts are made anew (eglTerminate,
eglInitialize), each view that had a surface gets one, and the engine
stands again. The windows are then posted the message registered by the
name "FlutterWindowsEglContextRestored", WPARAM 1 where it renders again
and 0 where not.

A backing store of a lost context is collected without OpenGL: the same
numbers may name other objects in the context made anew.

FlutterDesktopGLContextWasLost tells the engine of a loss heard by other
means; a library that exports it restores.

