+// [anicel 0005] Tells this process's engine that its OpenGL context is
+// lost, as an EGL call that fails by EGL_CONTEXT_LOST tells it -- for a loss
+// heard by other means (a runner's own device on the screen's adapter,
+// removed with it, while the engine made no call that failed) and for a
+// test. The windows of the process are posted the message registered by the
+// name "FlutterWindowsEglContextLost" -- once, till the engine stands again
+// -- the engine makes its contexts anew, and the windows are posted the
+// message registered by the name "FlutterWindowsEglContextRestored" (WPARAM
+// 1 where the engine renders again, 0 where not). Returns at once; the rest
+// follows on the platform thread.
+//
+// A library that exports this is one whose engine restores: a runner may
+// tell by looking the name up.
+FLUTTER_EXPORT void FlutterDesktopGLContextWasLost();
+
 FLUTTER_EXPORT void FlutterDesktopEngineReloadSystemFonts(
     FlutterDesktopEngineRef engine);
 
